    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm seeing some significant latency spikes in our production Kubernetes cluster during peak load. Specifically, we're seeing a bottleneck in the service mesh layer when handling inter-service communication via mTLS. We've ruled out resource exhaustion on the worker nodes. Could you help me troubleshoot potential configuration issues in the sidecar proxy injection or suggest how to optimize the handshake overhead?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Check your Istio configuration for excessive `forwardProxy` settings or overly strict mutual TLS policies that force full certificate chains during every request, which can significantly increase handshake latency. You can reduce overhead by disabling certificate pinning for internal traffic and configuring `maxInboundStreamsPerTransport` on your sidecars to prevent connection logjams during grid congestion. Additionally, verify that your mTLS policy isn't defaulting to `ISTIO_MUTUAL` without `PERMITTED_ISSUER`, as this can cause unexpected retries that load nodes unnecessarily.",
      "source": "target",
